Closing Thought
Scope is the map of who can see what, and for how long. var, let, and const just change how thick the walls are. Hoisting and the TDZ describe when a name becomes usable. Closures are what happens when a wall stays standing even after the room around it has been demolished.
Once you can draw the boxes, JavaScript stops feeling like magic — it starts feeling like architecture.
